{%- comment -%}
  Accessible icon-only button
  WCAG 1.1.1 Non-text Content, 4.1.2 Name Role Value, 2.5.8 Target Size

  Usage:

    {% render 'a11y-icon-button',
       icon: 'cart',
       label: 'Open cart drawer',
       controls: 'CartDrawer',
       expanded: false %}

  Why visually hidden text rather than aria-label:

  - It is translated by browser page translation. aria-label frequently is not.
  - It survives an icon set that fails to load.
  - Voice control users say the visible text. When aria-label differs from the
    visible label, "click cart" stops working. That mismatch is its own
    failure under 2.5.3 Label in Name.
  - It is visible in the DOM to whoever maintains this template next.

  Header icon buttons (cart, search, account, menu) are the highest volume
  source of unnamed controls on Shopify themes. One shared snippet fixes all
  of them at once and stops the problem returning.

  The label is escaped. It is usually a literal in the template, but it is also
  the obvious place for a merchant-editable string to arrive from a section
  setting, and an apostrophe in an unescaped attribute is how that goes wrong.
{%- endcomment -%}

<button
  type="button"
  class="a11y-icon-button"
  {% if controls %}aria-controls="{{ controls }}"{% endif %}
  {% unless expanded == nil %}aria-expanded="{{ expanded | default: false }}"{% endunless %}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The icon is chosen with a case block and not by building the snippet name
    from the icon parameter. Liquid's render tag takes a string literal: it does
    not accept a variable and it does not accept a filtered expression, so
    building a name with append resolves to nothing, renders nothing, and
    reports no error. The button then has an accessible name and no glyph, which
    looks like a missing icon file and is diagnosed as one.

    The snippet names on the right are Dawn's. Change them to match the theme.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- case icon -%}
    {%- when 'cart' -%}
      {%- render 'icon-cart' -%}
    {%- when 'search' -%}
      {%- render 'icon-search' -%}
    {%- when 'account' -%}
      {%- render 'icon-account' -%}
    {%- when 'menu' -%}
      {%- render 'icon-hamburger' -%}
    {%- when 'close' -%}
      {%- render 'icon-close' -%}
  {%- endcase -%}
  <span class="visually-hidden">{{ label | escape }}</span>
</button>

{%- style -%}
  /* The glyph stays whatever size the design calls for. The target is grown
     to the 24 by 24 CSS px that 2.5.8 requires at Level AA. Note that the AA
     minimum is 24, not 44. 44 is 2.5.5 at Level AAA and the Apple guideline,
     and it is very often misattributed to 2.5.8 in audit reports. */
  .a11y-icon-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-width: 24px;
    min-height: 24px;
    padding: 0.5rem;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .a11y-icon-button:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
